but we decided not to work

00:27:37.810 --> 00:27:39.630
in those because the classification

00:27:39.630 --> 00:27:43.060
of the parties becomes more complicated.

00:27:43.060 --> 00:27:46.700
A lot of for example,
congressional candidates

00:27:46.700 --> 00:27:49.750
did not have a very clear
agenda that will allow us,

00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:51.370
or enable us to kind of classify

00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:53.817
them as either center, left or right,

00:27:53.817 --> 00:27:57.180
but they have conflicted
policies that made it very hard

00:27:57.180 --> 00:27:58.700
for us to make a clear classification

00:27:58.700 --> 00:28:00.010
of their political orientation

00:28:00.010 --> 00:28:01.650
and so that's why we decided just to stay

00:28:01.650 --> 00:28:03.563
with this three elections.

00:28:05.210 --> 00:28:08.230
All right, so in general, what we found

00:28:09.130 --> 00:28:13.047
is that whenever the predictive
Venezuelan inflows increase

00:28:13.047 --> 00:28:14.410
in one standard deviation,

00:28:14.410 --> 00:28:16.530
we see across all of the elections

00:28:16.530 --> 00:28:20.530
so we examine larger
political participation,

00:28:20.530 --> 00:28:22.320
lower participate, or no longer support

00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:24.210
towards the left-wing political ideologies

00:28:24.210 --> 00:28:25.790
and larger towards right-wing.

00:28:25.790 --> 00:28:27.070
And just to kind of give you an overview

00:28:27.070 --> 00:28:29.100
of how large these effects are.

00:28:29.100 --> 00:28:30.670
The main support for the left

00:28:30.670 --> 00:28:32.720
for the first round presidential elections

00:28:32.720 --> 00:28:34.230
was zero point ten.

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:37.090
And the effect that we're
observing when we increase

00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:40.220
our measure of predictive
Venezuelan inflows

00:28:40.220 --> 00:28:43.110
in one standard deviation
is a change we observe

00:28:43.110 --> 00:28:45.260
a reduction of 0.9 percentage points.

00:28:45.260 --> 00:28:48.010
In other words, this is a 10% deviation

00:28:48.010 --> 00:28:51.130
from the mean support for
left-wing political ideology.

00:28:51.130 --> 00:28:53.320
So these are large impacts.

00:28:53.320 --> 00:28:55.380
And it is important to
kind of take into account

00:28:55.380 --> 00:28:57.770
that since the support for left

00:28:57.770 --> 00:28:59.550
is not that large in Colombia

00:28:59.550 --> 00:29:02.393
we're talking about very,
very important changes.

00:29:03.310 --> 00:29:06.520
So before I move on to talk
a lot about the mechanisms

00:29:06.520 --> 00:29:09.570
I wanted to kind of
mention two robustness test

00:29:09.570 --> 00:29:11.540
that we kind of run to test

00:29:11.540 --> 00:29:12.730
whether this was actually robust,

00:29:12.730 --> 00:29:14.600
these effects that I just showed you.

00:29:14.600 --> 00:29:16.410
So one was that we, yeah.

00:29:16.410 --> 00:29:19.930
- We have a question before
you do that which is,

00:29:19.930 --> 00:29:24.000
if the right-wing in Colombia
has a strong anti-immigration?

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:25.670
- Oh, great question.

00:29:25.670 --> 00:29:30.160
Let me just kinda talk about
this in a couple of slides.

00:29:30.160 --> 00:29:31.750
I'm going to on and talk about this,

00:29:31.750 --> 00:29:33.607
but no, the short answer is no.

00:29:33.607 --> 00:29:35.270
I will talk about that in a second.

00:29:35.270 --> 00:29:37.340
I will have a slide of that.

00:29:37.340 --> 00:29:39.500
So I don't want to lose a lot of time

00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:41.280
in this robustness test
but basically what we did

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:45.700
is we had a lot of concerns about the fact

00:29:45.700 --> 00:29:48.553
that maybe the departments
or the municipalities

00:29:48.553 --> 00:29:50.960
that were located in the
border with Venezuela

00:29:50.960 --> 00:29:52.010
had a different behavior.

00:29:52.010 --> 00:29:55.160
Basically they were more
pro-migrant or less pro-migrant

00:29:55.160 --> 00:29:57.870
because they see or have
more exposure to migrants.

00:29:57.870 --> 00:29:59.720
And so for that what we did is we run

00:29:59.720 --> 00:30:01.990
our estimates excluding
different departments

00:30:01.990 --> 00:30:04.570
of the country, one at a time
and we run everything again,

00:30:04.570 --> 00:30:07.240
and we find very robust
effects of everything

00:30:07.240 --> 00:30:08.740
that I've showed you.

00:30:08.740 --> 00:30:10.880
Another thing that we did is we say, okay,

00:30:10.880 --> 00:30:13.300
maybe this instrument or this
variable is not a good proxy

00:30:13.300 --> 00:30:15.860
of Venezuelan migration so
let's use a different one.

00:30:15.860 --> 00:30:17.080
What if we use just distance

00:30:17.080 --> 00:30:19.360
to the main border crossing locations

00:30:20.270 --> 00:30:22.033
in the Colombia-Venezuelan border.

00:30:23.200 --> 00:30:24.940
And for that, we calculated the distance

00:30:24.940 --> 00:30:28.130
of each municipality to each
of these border crossings

00:30:28.130 --> 00:30:29.580
and we ran everything again,

00:30:29.580 --> 00:30:31.400
and the results are very, very similar.

00:30:31.400 --> 00:30:35.750
In fact, we actually found that
there is a large correlation

00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:37.160
between the variable that we're using

00:30:37.160 --> 00:30:39.490
and the distance to the border,

00:30:39.490 --> 00:30:41.913
so that the results are
also very, very similar.

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:45.990
Okay, so now we're gonna
move on to try to see

00:30:45.990 --> 00:30:47.270
what could be driving this effect.

00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:49.410
So remember there are
three possible mechanisms

00:30:49.410 --> 00:30:50.243
that we wanted to explore

00:30:50.243 --> 00:30:53.510
and one is maybe this is
just economic effects, right?

00:30:53.510 --> 00:30:54.870
Maybe this is just migrants

00:30:54.870 --> 00:30:57.320
are having a negative
impact only for example,

00:30:57.320 --> 00:30:59.420
labor outcomes and we want to see

00:30:59.420 --> 00:31:02.620
whether that there is some
evidence of that truly happening.

00:31:02.620 --> 00:31:04.860
So the first thing is
exactly that checking

00:31:04.860 --> 00:31:08.910
whether Venezuelan migration
has affected outcomes

00:31:08.910 --> 00:31:11.480
in the formal or informal sector.

00:31:11.480 --> 00:31:14.020
And for that, would we use
the labor force surveys

00:31:14.020 --> 00:31:16.810
in Colombia and we basically tested

00:31:16.810 --> 00:31:20.140
the main labor outcomes,
hours, work, wages

00:31:20.140 --> 00:31:23.350
and unemployment in the
formal and informal sector.

00:31:23.350 --> 00:31:26.060
And here I'm showing you the results.

00:31:26.060 --> 00:31:28.303
It's a very similar
identification strategy.

00:31:29.140 --> 00:31:32.590
And what we see overwhelmingly
is that whenever there

00:31:32.590 --> 00:31:35.713
or in the municipalities
where there is a larger inflow

00:31:35.713 --> 00:31:39.470
of Venezuelan migrants,
individuals, Colombia nationals

00:31:39.470 --> 00:31:44.470
are working more they have
a larger unemployment rates.

00:31:44.750 --> 00:31:47.990
And we also see some, let's
say suggestive evidence

00:31:47.990 --> 00:31:50.590
that wages are dropping,
but it's not enough

00:31:50.590 --> 00:31:52.690
to identify a statistically
significant effect.

00:31:52.690 --> 00:31:55.540
So this is somehow saying, okay, yes,

00:31:55.540 --> 00:31:57.670
there is something on
the economic environment

00:31:57.670 --> 00:32:00.890
that might be driving voting behaviors.

00:32:00.890 --> 00:32:03.030
And then we said, okay,

00:32:03.030 --> 00:32:06.730
what else could be a main
important economic effect

00:32:06.730 --> 00:32:07.563
that migrants

00:32:07.563 --> 00:32:09.960
could have that may be
driving voting decisions?

00:32:09.960 --> 00:32:11.990
And we thought another very important one

00:32:11.990 --> 00:32:13.530
was a fiscal burden.

00:32:13.530 --> 00:32:18.140
So in the sense that maybe
individuals are paying more taxes

00:32:18.140 --> 00:32:21.290
or the government is sending
more money to those regions

00:32:21.290 --> 00:32:23.230
that are actually receiving more migrants.

00:32:23.230 --> 00:32:26.350
And for that, we use municipal data

00:32:26.350 --> 00:32:30.520
on tax income per capita,
and the government transfers

00:32:31.530 --> 00:32:33.930
from the central government
to the municipalities.

00:32:33.930 --> 00:32:35.430
And we see evidences both.

00:32:35.430 --> 00:32:38.880
So we do see that it seems
that at a per capita level,

00:32:38.880 --> 00:32:42.780
individuals are actually paying more taxes

00:32:42.780 --> 00:32:46.000
and also the central government
is sending more money

00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:48.570
to these municipalities that
are receiving more migrants.

00:32:48.570 --> 00:32:52.450
And so overall issue
resolved kind of give us

00:32:52.450 --> 00:32:53.283
a very good understanding

00:32:53.283 --> 00:32:56.030
that there's something going
on in the economic dimension

00:32:56.030 --> 00:32:57.820
that might be driving voting effects.

00:32:57.820 --> 00:33:01.280
So we cannot discourage, or discard

00:33:03.480 --> 00:33:04.990
this socio-economic hypothesis

00:33:04.990 --> 00:33:08.060
that this is very something
here at least in Colombia.

00:33:08.060 --> 00:33:10.580
So the second hypothesis
was the cultural hypothesis,

00:33:10.580 --> 00:33:13.030
which is very much in line with a question

00:33:13.030 --> 00:33:15.900
that I just received
from Maria Teresa saying,

00:33:15.900 --> 00:33:20.680
is it true that right-wing
ideologies are anti-immigrant?

00:33:20.680 --> 00:33:24.230
And so for this part of the analysis,

00:33:24.230 --> 00:33:29.070
we're not gonna be able to
offer a statistical analysis,

00:33:29.070 --> 00:33:32.750
but we will kind of
talk to you why we think

00:33:32.750 --> 00:33:34.020
or try to convince you why we think

00:33:34.020 --> 00:33:35.040
this is not the main driver.

00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:38.380
So the first thing is that
no, right-wing ideologists

00:33:38.380 --> 00:33:40.710
in Colombia are not
typically anti-immigrant.

00:33:40.710 --> 00:33:44.860
So in fact, the current
president of Colombia Iva Duque

00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:48.560
is a very pro-immigrant president.

00:33:48.560 --> 00:33:51.930
So he has been supporting
a very large amnesty

00:33:51.930 --> 00:33:55.100
that has regularized Venezuelan migrants.

00:33:55.100 --> 00:33:58.480
He has also given them
a very generous access

00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:00.650
to social safety nets and recently

00:34:00.650 --> 00:34:05.650
to unlimited health coverage
to any migrants in Colombia.

00:34:08.170 --> 00:34:10.580
And I think this is an important
thing to take into account

00:34:10.580 --> 00:34:13.970
because when we are kind
of ringing conclusions

00:34:13.970 --> 00:34:17.710
from the north to the
south, we cannot translate

00:34:17.710 --> 00:34:21.440
these right and left-wing
orientations in the same way.

00:34:21.440 --> 00:34:23.650
So each country has their different views

00:34:23.650 --> 00:34:28.010
or different political, let's
say agendas identifying left

00:34:28.010 --> 00:34:29.070
and right and in Colombia

00:34:29.070 --> 00:34:32.903
particularly right-wing
ideologies are not anti-immigrant.

00:34:34.560 --> 00:34:38.020
Another important thing
to kind of mention here

00:34:38.020 --> 00:34:41.030
why we do not think
this cultural hypothesis

00:34:41.030 --> 00:34:43.500
could be driving our effects
is as Colombia-Venezuela

00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:45.520
are culturally very similar.

00:34:45.520 --> 00:34:48.340
So Colombians and
Venezuelans speak Spanish

00:34:48.340 --> 00:34:52.760
and we were part of a same
country up until the 1831.

00:34:52.760 --> 00:34:57.590
We or the very large vast
majority of Colombians Venezuelans

00:34:57.590 --> 00:35:00.490
have the same religion, eat similar foods.

00:35:00.490 --> 00:35:02.130
And so for all of these reasons,

00:35:02.130 --> 00:35:07.130
it's really hard to envision
that the voting behaviors

00:35:07.260 --> 00:35:08.880
or changing voting behaviors
are actually driven

00:35:08.880 --> 00:35:12.730
by a cultural, let's
say xenophobic reaction.

00:35:12.730 --> 00:35:14.150
But of course, this is not something

00:35:14.150 --> 00:35:15.900
that we can prove it statistically.

00:35:17.600 --> 00:35:20.590
And so the last mechanism that we wanted

00:35:20.590 --> 00:35:22.730
to kind of bring forth is what we call

00:35:22.730 --> 00:35:25.090
the electoral manipulation hypothesis.

00:35:25.090 --> 00:35:27.920
And again, this is this
idea that the white

00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:30.260
might be using the migration presence

00:35:30.260 --> 00:35:32.780
or the large migration
flows to say, if you vote

00:35:32.780 --> 00:35:35.520
for the left, we are going
to become the country

00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:38.110
who actually expelled all
of it's migrants, right?

00:35:38.110 --> 00:35:40.540
Or in other words, the right saying,

00:35:40.540 --> 00:35:44.220
we're going to become Venezuela
if you vote for the left.

00:35:44.220 --> 00:35:47.070
And I'm showing you just
hear some anecdotal evidence

00:35:47.070 --> 00:35:50.550
of banners posted all across the country

00:35:50.550 --> 00:35:52.860
in which there were
different messages suggesting

00:35:52.860 --> 00:35:55.363
this idea saying, for example,
I don't want to leave us

00:35:55.363 --> 00:35:57.420
a Venezuelan, if you
don't want to leave us

00:35:57.420 --> 00:35:59.200
a Venezuelan vote for Duque

00:35:59.200 --> 00:36:01.593
which was a right-wing
president candidate.

00:36:04.500 --> 00:36:06.826
Vote for that Colombia, yeah. Sorry.

00:36:06.826 --> 00:36:08.940
- [Mushfiq] I'm Mushfiq,
if I can just interrupt.

00:36:08.940 --> 00:36:11.230
I'm just confused by
the word manipulation,

00:36:11.230 --> 00:36:14.020
because manipulation sounds a lot stronger

00:36:14.020 --> 00:36:17.480
than regular messaging, right?

00:36:17.480 --> 00:36:19.410
Like almost like cheating.

00:36:19.410 --> 00:36:20.560
That's not what you mean you just know

00:36:20.560 --> 00:36:23.150
that they're changing their
messaging to take advantage of-

00:36:23.150 --> 00:36:25.350
- Absolutely, I'm so sorry.
Yes, you're absolutely right.

00:36:25.350 --> 00:36:26.630
Yeah. I haven't thought about that.

00:36:26.630 --> 00:36:29.180
Yes, manipulation is, we're
not using this word to say

00:36:29.180 --> 00:36:31.700
that this is illegal or cheating.

00:36:31.700 --> 00:36:32.580
No, not at all.

00:36:32.580 --> 00:36:35.720
It's just like a message
they are kind of using

00:36:35.720 --> 00:36:40.720
